    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0330" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg224"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-10-04">October 4,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 195]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    telegram of the 28th ultimo, reading as follows:<anchor n="a" xml:id="d204-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>You will continue pressure for the customs-houses, and you will inform the
                    Chinese Government that the demand as to Newchwang will be renewed with
                    increased emphasis if the present condition is allowed to continue.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d204-f1" n="a" xml:id="d204-f1-content">
                <p>Supra.</p>
